  "query_preview": "(Today through Thursday)...\nIssued at 258 AM EST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nToday through tonight...\n\nLatest surface and satellite observations depict extensive \nclouds across the region as a system moves through region. An \nassociated cold front currently centered near northern portions of \ncentral Indiana is quickly pushing southward. Low-level convergence \nalong the boundary has promoted scattered light showers. Patchy \ndrizzle has also been reported at times ahead of the cold front. \nLook for scattered light showers or drizzle to remain possible \nthrough about daybreak drier air begins to filter in.\n\nAt least partial clearing is expected during the day due to cold air \nadvection behind the front. However, mostly cloudy skies should \npersist for much of the day aided by lake enhanced low-level \nmoisture. Isolated lake enhanced showers or patchy drizzle cannot be \nruled out either, mainly across far northern counties. Limited \ndiurnal heating from mostly cloudy skies on top of continued cold \nair advection will keep highs in the low-mid 50s. Clearing skies \nlate in the day into the evening along with winds becoming light \novernight supports efficient radiational cooling. Look for lows to \ndrop into the upper 20s to mid 30s tonight. \n\nSaturday through the middle of next week...\n\nQuiet weather conditions are expected this weekend through the \nmiddle of next week as surface high pressure generally remains in \ncontrol. Ensemble guidance depicts a few subtle systems pushing weak \ncold fronts through the region during this period. Gulf moisture \nremaining cutoff will keep these fronts moisture starved though \nallowing for dry conditions to persist. \n\nLook for highs to remain in the low to mid 50s Saturday before \nreturn flow helps temperatures moderate into early next week. Highs \non Sunday will generally range from the upper 50s to low 60s with \nwidespread highs in the 60s to start the work week. A cold front \nmoving through midweek should cool highs back down into the 50s by \nThursday. Widespread lows in the upper 20s to low 30s are expected \nSaturday night into Sunday.",
